.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-CAPSULE 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-capsule
.Nd the noqtis capsule format, version 1
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A capsule is a folder that holds the files of a result together with
.Pa noqtis.json ,
the manifest, and
.Pa noqtis.sig ,
the seal, both at the top of the folder.
The manifest lists every file with its size and two digests; the seal
signs the manifest's exact bytes with a post-quantum signature.
.Pp
The key words MUST, MUST NOT, SHOULD and MAY are to be read as in
RFC 2119 and RFC 8174.
.Ss Canonical JSON
Both files MUST be JSON (RFC 8259) in the canonical form of RFC 8785
(JCS): UTF-8, no whitespace outside strings, object members sorted by the
UTF-16 code units of their names, strings with the minimal escapes, and
numbers in the shortest form that round-trips.
A checker MUST reject a file that is not byte-identical to its own
canonical form, has a duplicate member name, or is not valid UTF-8.
.Ss The manifest, noqtis.json
An object with exactly these members:
.Bl -tag -width "created"
.It Cm created
A string: the creation time, RFC 3339 in UTC,
.Ql YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ
with optional fractional seconds before the
.Ql Z .
.It Cm files
An array with one object per file, sorted by the bytes of
.Cm path ,
with no path twice.
Each object has exactly:
.Bl -tag -width "sha3_256"
.It Cm path
the file's path relative to the capsule folder, a string;
.It Cm sha256
its SHA-256, 64 lower-case hex digits;
.It Cm sha3_256
its SHA3-256, 64 lower-case hex digits;
.It Cm size
its size in bytes, an integer from 0 to 2^53\-1.
.El
.It Cm format
The string
.Ql noqtis-capsule-1 .
.It Cm meta
Optional: any JSON object, at most 1 MiB, opaque to noqtis.
.El
.Pp
Because of the canonical order, the manifest always reads
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"created":...,"files":[{"path":...,"sha256":...,
"sha3_256":...,"size":...},...],"format":"noqtis-capsule-1"
[,"meta":{...}]}
.Ed
.Ss Paths
A path MUST use
.Ql /
between names, MUST NOT start with
.Ql / ,
and MUST be in normal form: no empty segment and no
.Ql \&. .
Every name (segment) MUST be valid UTF-8 without overlong forms or
surrogates, MUST NOT be empty,
.Ql \&.
or
.Ql .. ,
and MUST NOT contain a control character (U+0000 to U+001F, U+007F),
.Ql / ,
.Ql \e
or
.Ql \&: .
Two paths of one capsule MUST NOT differ only in ASCII case.
A path MUST be at most 4096 bytes.
.Pp
.Pa noqtis.json
and
.Pa noqtis.sig
at the top of the folder are not listed.
Only regular files are listed; folders are implied by the paths, so an
empty folder is not recorded.
.Ss The seal, noqtis.sig
An object with exactly these members:
.Bl -tag -width "manifest_sha256"
.It Cm alg
The signature algorithm, as
.Fn nqsname
.Pq Xr nqsign 3
names it, for example
.Ql ML-DSA-65
or
.Ql SLH-DSA-SHAKE-128s .
.It Cm context
The FIPS 204/205 context string the signature was made with, at most 255
bytes.
A sealer SHOULD use
.Ql noqtis-capsule-1 ;
.Xr nqseal 3
always does.
.It Cm format
The string
.Ql noqtis-seal-1 .
.It Cm manifest_sha256
The SHA-256 of the exact bytes of
.Pa noqtis.json ,
64 lower-case hex digits.
.It Cm public_key
The signer's public key, base64 (RFC 4648 section 4, padded, no line
breaks) of the standard's encoding.
.It Cm signature
The pure ML-DSA or SLH-DSA signature over the exact bytes of
.Pa noqtis.json
with that context, base64 likewise.
.It Cm timestamp
Optional: base64 of an RFC 3161 time-stamp token whose message imprint is
the hash (SHA-256, SHA-384 or SHA-512) of the decoded
.Cm signature
bytes.
.El
.Ss Limits
A checker MUST refuse, with a failing check and never by truncating:
.Pa noqtis.json
over 512 MiB (its size is checked before it is read, and again if it
grows while being read);
.Pa noqtis.sig
over 1 MiB;
.Cm meta
over 1 MiB; more than 2,000,000 files; a path over 4096 bytes; folders
more than 64 levels deep.
JSON nesting is limited to 64 levels.
.Ss Sealing
A sealer MUST list every entry of the folder without following links and
MUST refuse to seal a folder that holds a symbolic link, a Windows
reparse point, a special file (device, pipe, socket), a name the rules
above refuse, two paths that differ only in ASCII case, or anything over
a limit.
It MUST verify the new signature before writing the seal.
.Ss Checking
A checker MUST:
.Bl -enum
.It
check that both files are canonical with exactly the fields above and
the right formats, and that
.Cm alg
is known and
.Cm public_key
and
.Cm signature
have the algorithm's sizes;
.It
check that the SHA-256 of
.Pa noqtis.json
equals
.Cm manifest_sha256 ;
.It
verify
.Cm signature
over the exact bytes of
.Pa noqtis.json
with
.Cm context ,
using the trusted public key when the caller gave one (and then require
that
.Cm public_key
equal it), otherwise
.Cm public_key ,
and say which;
.It
for every listed file: require it to exist, to be a regular file reached
without following a link, and to have the listed size, SHA-256 and
SHA3-256;
.It
fail on every regular file present but not listed, every link, special
file or refused name in the folder, every path out of order, listed
twice, not in normal form, or differing from another only in case;
.It
when trust anchors for time-stamping authorities are given, require a
.Cm timestamp
whose imprint matches and whose token verifies, with the TSA certificate
path valid at the token's genTime, under one of them; when none are given,
fail a
.Cm timestamp
that is present, since it cannot be checked.
.El
.Pp
A capsule passes only when every check passes.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa noqtis.json
the manifest
.It Pa noqtis.sig
the seal
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A manifest (one line in the file; broken here for width):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"created":"2026-10-28T23:35:26Z","files":[{"path":"data/in.csv",
"sha256":"5be08c96...","sha3_256":"cec130cc...","size":4},
{"path":"report.txt","sha256":"8e54b0ca...","sha3_256":"cfd6402f...",
"size":2}],"format":"noqtis-capsule-1","meta":{"project":"demo"}}
.Ed
.Pp
Its seal:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{"alg":"ML-DSA-65","context":"noqtis-capsule-1",
"format":"noqtis-seal-1","manifest_sha256":"9f322e95...",
"public_key":"1qWycP39...","signature":"..."}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-check 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-seal 1 ,
.Xr nqchk 3 ,
.Xr nqchkt 3 ,
.Xr nqseal 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%R RFC 8785
.%T JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS)
.%D June 2020
.Re
.Rs
.%R RFC 3161
.%T Internet X.509 Public Key Infrastructure Time-Stamp Protocol (TSP)
.%D August 2001
.Re
.Rs
